 throne."	 王座。
Press any key to continue.	請按任意鍵繼續。
There is no need to bow again.	不需要再鞠躬了。
Your concern for the old king won't allow you to move.	你對這位老國王的擔憂讓你動彈不得。
    Thank you for playing             King's Quest                     from               Ken and Roberta Williams     Sol Ackerman   Chris Iden           Jeff Stephenson                 Mark Crowe            Bob Ballew   Mikel Knight     Susan Lee    Russ Truelove         Larry Weissenborn   	    Thank you for playing             King's Quest                     from               Ken and Roberta Williams     Sol Ackerman   Chris Iden           Jeff Stephenson                 Mark Crowe            Bob Ballew   Mikel Knight     Susan Lee    Russ Truelove         Larry Weissenborn   
The king cannot talk right now.	國王現在無法交談。
That is no way to try and address King Edward.	你不能用這種方式對愛德華國王說話。
The spell to make you invisible has expired and you are once again visible.	隱身魔法已經失效，你再次現形了。
That man is the King.	那個人就是國王。
The light from the oil lamp is rather dim in the dark interior of the castle.	油燈的光線在城堡幽暗的內部顯得相當微弱。
The long marble hall has a cold, dreary feeling.	這條長長的大理石走廊給人一種冰冷、陰鬱的感覺。
There is nobody in the armor.	盔甲裡沒有人。
This is the armor of one of King Edward's knights from years ago.	這是愛德華國王麾下一名騎士多年前留下的盔甲。
The armor is firmly mounted to the wall.	這副盔甲牢牢固定在牆上。
You should know you can't walk on clouds.	你應該知道，人是無法走在雲上的。
These flowers look different than any you have ever seen before.	這些花朵看起來和你以前見過的都不一樣。
You'll have to keep yourself out of the clouds!	你得讓自己遠離雲朵才行！
These are very unusual looking trees.	這些樹看起來非常不尋常。
You are fortunate that you have the magic shield or this giant would cause problems for you.	幸虧你有靈盾在身，否則這個巨人會給你帶來大麻煩。
The magic chest appears to have been fashioned from ebony and rimmed on the edges with gold.	這只金盒子似乎是用烏木打造，邊緣鑲著金邊。
There is no chest around here to get.	這附近沒有盒子可以拿。
Very carefully, you slip the magic chest from the sleeping giant's arms.	你小心翼翼地，從熟睡巨人的懷裡抽出了金盒子。
There is no way you can get the chest from here!	你沒辦法從這裡拿到那個盒子！
You put the pebble in the sling, take careful aim, and luckily hit the giant in the forehead!  He falls down dead.	你把鵝卵石放進投石器，仔細瞄準，幸運地擊中了巨人的額頭！他應聲倒地身亡。
It would be rather cowardly of you to kill a giant while he is asleep!	趁巨人熟睡時殺他，未免太卑鄙了！
You have no sling!	你身上沒有投石器！
I don't believe it!  How could you miss something so big?	真不敢相信！這麼大的目標你怎麼會射不中？
You have no dagger!	你身上沒有短刀！
There is no reason to kill the giant.	沒有理由殺這個巨人。
The giant has been slain by a little pebble to the forehead.	巨人被一顆小小的鵝卵石擊中額頭，就此喪命。
Be a little more careful next time.  This giant is mean!	下次小心一點。這個巨人很兇惡！
You know you can't walk on clouds.	你知道人是無法走在雲上的。
What luck!  The huge giant fell fast asleep!	運氣真好！巨大的巨人沉沉睡去了！
The giant is sleeping with a chest.	巨人抱著一只盒子睡著了。
The giant lies dead on the ground and there is a chest beside him.	巨人倒臥在地上死了，身旁還有一只盒子。
The giant is to close for the slingshot to be effective.  I would suggest you RUN!	巨人離你太近了，投石器派不上用場。我建議你快跑！
The dark cave burrows its way into a steep mountain.	這個黑暗的洞穴深入陡峭的山中。
The mountain is too steep to climb.	這座山太陡峭，無法攀爬。
You are near the top of a very high mountain.  It steeply descends toward a valley floor.	你正身處一座高山的頂端附近，山勢陡峭地向下延伸至山谷。
You are in the Land of the Clouds.  It is rumored that a giant lives here.	你身處雲之國，傳說有個巨人住在這上面。
Oops, you've missed the edge and fallen through the  clouds.	哎呀，你沒踩穩邊緣，摔穿雲層掉了下去。
These are the most unusual looking trees.	這些樹看起來奇特無比。
These are unusual looking flowers.	這些花朵看起來很不尋常。
You should know that it is not possible to walk on clouds!	你應該知道，人是不可能走在雲上的！
This is very strange vegetation.	這是非常奇特的植物。
Oops!  You've missed the edge and fallen through the clouds.	哎呀！你沒踩穩邊緣，摔穿雲層掉了下去。
Its trunk has a large hole in the base.	樹幹底部有一個大洞。
You notice a sling in the hole in the tree.	你注意到樹洞裡有一把投石器。
It is empty.	裡面是空的。
This sling is made of very stretchy leather.	這把投石器是用非常有彈性的皮革做的。
You reach into the hole and pull out the leather sling.	你把手伸進洞裡，拉出那把皮革投石器。
You can't see into the hole from here.	你從這裡看不進那個洞裡。
Why?  What sling?	為什麼？什麼投石器？
You've fallen through the clouds!  Cloud walking is for the birds.	你摔穿雲層掉了下去！走在雲上這種事，還是留給鳥兒吧。
These are strange looking trees.	這些樹看起來很奇怪。
You need to be closer to try.	你得靠近一點才能嘗試。
There is a rather large bird's nest here.	這裡有一個相當大的鳥巢。
There is a pure golden egg lying in the nest!	鳥巢裡躺著一顆純金打造的蛋！
The nest is empty.	鳥巢是空的。
The golden egg is smooth and shiny.	這顆金蛋光滑又閃亮。
You already have the golden egg from the nest.	你已經拿到鳥巢裡的金蛋了。
There is no egg here to get.	這裡沒有蛋可以拿。
The golden egg is so heavy you almost drop it.	這顆金蛋重得你差點沒拿穩。
You can't get the egg from here!	你沒辦法從這裡拿到那顆蛋！
Apparently you lost your grip while climbing this tree and you fall to the hard earth below.	看來你爬這棵樹時沒抓穩，摔到了下方堅硬的地面上。
So you're walking on clouds, huh?  Unfortunately, that's an impossible task that cost you your life!	所以你想走在雲上，是吧？可惜，這是件不可能的任務，也讓你賠上了性命！
As the wicked witch flew over her house, she dropped you... into her cage!  If you can't get out, you may become the secret ingredient in this witches' brew!	邪惡的巫婆飛過她的房子上空時，把你丟了下去……正好落進她的籠子裡！要是逃不出去，你可能會變成這鍋巫婆濃湯裡的神秘配料！
Surprise!  Surprise!  The wicked witch is home and now she's after you!	沒想到吧！沒想到吧！邪惡的巫婆在家，現在她盯上你了！
This is not a good place to give up your protection!	這裡可不是放棄你護身之物的好地方！
The witch mutters, "I am going to get my oven ready to cook someone for dinner (yum)."	巫婆喃喃道：「我要去把烤爐準備好，煮個人來當晚餐（嗯，真香）。」
The witch mumbles, "After I get the oven nice and hot, I will be ready to have someone for dinner (giggle)."	巫婆嘀咕著：「等我把烤爐燒得夠熱，就能請人來吃晚餐了（咯咯）。」
The witch mutters, "The oven is heating up nicely.  I wonder who will be my dinner guest!"	巫婆喃喃道：「烤爐燒得正好，不知道誰會是我的晚餐貴客呢！」
The witch says, "My oven is now the perfect temperature. It is time to invite someone for dinner (cackle, cackle)!"	巫婆說：「我的烤爐現在溫度剛剛好，是時候邀請誰來吃晚餐了（咯咯笑）！」
Rats!  She has cast some spell to keep you from escaping!. The witch remarks, "Oh, how nice of you to come for dinner (cackle, cackle)"	糟了！她施了某種魔法讓你逃不掉！巫婆說道：「喔，你能來吃晚餐真是太好了（咯咯笑）」
She pokes and pinches you, then states, "This one is too scrawny, so it's into the cage until you fatten up (smack, yum)!"	她戳了戳你、又捏了捏你，接著說：「這個太瘦了，先關進籠子養胖再說吧（咂嘴，真香）！」
With a flash, you hear her joyously exclaim, "This has made me feel like flying!"	一陣閃光中，你聽見她欣喜地喊道：「這讓我感覺自己要飛起來了！」
Courageously, you manage to push the witch into the oven where she flashes and melts away into a harmless blob. Congratulations!	你鼓起勇氣，把巫婆推進了烤爐，她閃了一下，融化成一團無害的軟泥。恭喜你！
Try as you will to escape, your labor will be in vain.	任憑你怎麼掙扎逃脫，都是白費力氣。
It is fastened with a very strong lock.  There is no way for you to open it.	它被一個非常堅固的鎖鎖著，你沒辦法打開它。
This ugly old witch is one of the most hideous sights you have ever seen.  I would never trust her.	這個醜陋的老巫婆，是你見過最駭人的景象之一。我絕不會相信她。
There is no witch here.	這裡沒有巫婆。
You pluck the Swiss cheese from the shelf.	你從架上取下瑞士乳酪。
I don't see any here.	這裡沒看到。
You cannot see it from here.	你從這裡看不到它。
This cage will be your new home for the rest of your life.	這個籠子將成為你餘生的新家。
You look for a way to escape, but there is none.	你四處尋找逃脫的辦法，卻找不到任何出路。
It is an old wood stove, and very hot.  The fire must have been burning for some time.	這是一個老舊的柴爐，非常燙。爐火想必已經燒了一段時間。
It is made from rusty, but strong, iron bars.	它是用生鏽但堅固的鐵條做的。
You may have seen one in the other room, but I am not sure.	你或許在另一個房間見過一個，但我不太確定。
The oven is very, very hot.  Someone must have just put some wood in it.	烤爐非常非常燙，一定有人剛加了柴進去。
You open the door and see a roaring fire burning in the oven.	你打開爐門，看見烤爐裡烈火熊熊。
You are in no position to do that!	你現在沒辦法做這件事！
You are not close enough to touch it.	你離它不夠近，碰不到。
From here it would be rather difficult to open the oven.	從這裡要打開烤爐相當困難。
There is a note lying on top of it.	上面放著一張紙條。
That is the table where she eats her (gulp) food.	那是她（吞口水）吃飯的桌子。
The bed is not here.	床不在這裡。
You see the forest outside.	你看見外頭的森林。
There is little to see from here.	從這裡看不到什麼。
The note was here at one time, but now you can`t seem to locate it.	紙條原本在這裡，但現在你似乎找不到它了。
You cannot reach it from here.	你從這裡搆不到它。
You don't have the note.	你身上沒有那張紙條。
If I were you, I wouldn't try it!  This witch is mean!	如果我是你，我才不會嘗試呢！這個巫婆很兇惡！
The little house is surprisingly neat considering a wicked witch lives here.	考慮到這裡住著一個邪惡的巫婆，這間小屋出乎意料地整潔。
There is no witch here...RIGHT NOW!!	這裡沒有巫婆……目前是沒有！！
The witch is dead.	巫婆死了。
As soon as you entered the house the goat ran away.	你一走進屋裡，山羊就跑掉了。
You need to be more specific.	你需要說得更具體一點。
The old goat is afraid of the dark and decides to stay outside.	老山羊害怕黑暗，決定留在外面。
The stairs go up into the heart of the mountain.	階梯向上通往山的核心。
Oops!  Those stairs are pretty slippery, aren't they?	哎呀！這些階梯挺滑的，是吧？
The stairs are moss-covered and slippery.	階梯上長滿青苔，很滑。
Darn!  You slipped on the steep stairs.	糟糕！你在陡峭的階梯上滑倒了。
The stairs seem to go on forever.	這些階梯似乎沒有盡頭。
This is a shy little dwarf.  He is too quick to catch.	這是個害羞的小矮人，他動作太快，抓不到。
Look out!  You are too close to the edge!  Oh, oh, you fell!	小心！你離邊緣太近了！啊，糟了，你摔下去了！
The quick, little dwarf came by to see what you had-- nothing interested him.	動作敏捷的小矮人跑來看你有什麼東西——但沒有一樣讓他感興趣。
There is nobody here but you.	這裡除了你沒有別人。
The dwarf is not here for idle conversion.	矮人不是來這裡閒聊的。
The stairs descend into the lower reaches of the mountain.	階梯向下通往山的深處。
You can see sky, light, and smell clouds through the opening.	你能透過開口看見天空、光線，還能聞到雲的氣味。
Oh dear!  With a slip of the foot, you fall head over heels down the long stairway.	糟了！你腳下一滑，一路翻滾摔下這條長長的階梯。
If you were to jump or duck here you might fall.	你要是在這裡跳躍或蹲下，可能會摔下去。
With a wrong move, you fall dizzyingly to the ground.	一個錯誤的動作，你便天旋地轉地摔到地上。
The goat was quite hesitant about climbing that huge beanstalk!  You may have lost the goat.	山羊對爬上那根巨大的豆莖相當猶豫！你可能已經把山羊弄丟了。
You can no longer see the bottom... it seems to go  on forever!	你已經看不見底部了……看來這裡深不見底！
You have to be careful when you get so high on the foliage!	爬到葉叢這麼高的地方，你得小心一點！
Whoops!  You fall toward a distant earth.	哎呀！你朝著遙遠的地面墜落。
Your heart thuds.  Dare you climb into the clouds?	你的心怦怦直跳。你敢爬進雲層裡嗎？
It is a long, long way down....	那可是好長、好長的一段路……
